// fix-health-app-v2.4.23.cjs — Family Health Track v2.4.23 one-step fix
// Requires a project at v2.4.22 (re-run at v2.4.23 is fine — files already
// applied are skipped).
// Run from the project root (the folder with package.json) with:
//   node fix-health-app-v2.4.23.cjs
// What it does:
//   1. Backs up each changed file to <file>.bak (first run only)
//   2. Applies the v2.4.23 fix - the full start-to-finish re-check:
//      (a) Full re-check - Login to Admin, every screen walked
//          button by button: date/age guards, BP/glucose range
//          checks, reminders labelled device-only, guide-module
//          answers now persist per user (no more lost ticks).
//      (b) Compactness - denser layout everywhere: smaller Trends
//          hero card (one-row health-status pill), Database stat
//          cards two-per-row on phones, tighter paddings/gaps on
//          every module, admin and guide screen.
//      (c) Horizontal scroll - measured for real at 360px: the BMI
//          tooltip that stuck out past the viewport and the
//          squeezed datetime-local inputs in admin forms are fixed.
//      (d) Wording - "အကုန်" labels become "အားလုံး" (clinical
//          sentences and historical Version History entries untouched).
//   3. Runs npm install, typecheck (tsc), tests (vitest) and build
//   4. SELF-CLEAN: after the checks pass, deletes the .bak backups and
//      older fix scripts automatically (never verify.cjs, never itself)
// Safe to run twice: files already matching the new content are skipped.
// It does NOT touch your data, your Firebase project, or git.
// NOTE: this version does NOT change firestore.rules — nothing to publish
// in the Firebase Console after running.
